<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 10.014 percent from 9.984 percent at the previous auction on January 15.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: April 24, 1997 (April 17, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.014 percent (9.984)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 984.500 million (603.775 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.185 billion (1.177 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.501-10.196 percent (9.863-9.998)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.501-10.200 percent (9.863-10.099)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 147 (42)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 151 (156)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
